Subject: [PATCH v1 0/1] iio: light: stk3310: IRQ-less operation
To: Jonathan Cameron <jic23@kernel.org>
Cc: David Lechner <dlechner@baylibre.com>,
    Nuno Sá <nuno.sa@analog.com>,
    Andy Shevchenko <andy@kernel.org>,
    linux-iio@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

The stk3310 driver accepts devices without an interrupt, but still
enables the proximity interrupt in the chip and exposes event
attributes that can never fire. This makes IRQ-less (polled) devices
such as the STK36C61 on the Fairphone 6 event-free.

Tested on the Fairphone 6 with iio-sensor-proxy.

Development was assisted by an AI coding tool (see the Assisted-by tag).

Paul Schuldesz (1):
  iio: light: stk3310: Do not enable proximity interrupts without an IRQ

 drivers/iio/light/stk3310.c | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

